## Lore

The Aviane are winged, feathered humanoids from a world of peaks, gorges
and cliffs, where the ability to fly was the difference between eating
and starving. When a dying star''s shock wave began tearing their planet
apart, flocks escaped through the Rifts that opened in their skies, and
thousands arrived on Earth around the time of the Great Cataclysm.

After early years in the ruins of skyscrapers, most drifted west to the
Rockies and the canyons of Arizona and Utah, and they now live along the
western mountain chains from Alaska to Mexico. A large flock of several
hundred lives openly in and around Arzno, where engineers have built
cliffside aeries for them.

They are a little smaller than a man, with feathers on the head, neck,
upper arms and back. Males are brightly colored, from blue-jay blues to
cardinal red; females are tan and grey. Social, curious and quick to
trust, Aviane love company, aerial games and gossip, and adventurous ones
join mercenary bands, Reid''s Rangers, the Justice Rangers and even the
Cyber-Knights. The Coalition shoots them on sight, a lesson they learned
when a group that settled near Chi-Town was nearly wiped out.
', 'published', 'data-script'
